Conxian’s Protocol Architecture and Component Synergies
Conxian operates as a highly cohesive ecosystem, comprising several meticulously engineered repositories that enforce its strategic vision of institutional-grade security. Strict adherence to mainnet-ready branch promotion policies ensures that the architecture remains robust across all deployment surfaces.
Conxian Gateway: The Middleware Layer
The conxian-gateway is a production-ready (v0.1.5) Rust-based middleware application designed specifically to bridge Bitcoin and Stacks state logic with enterprise compliance frameworks. Recognizing that traditional finance requires standardized communication protocols, the Gateway natively supports ISO 20022 (pacs.008) banking-standard messaging. It simplifies the integration path for institutions and fintechs by providing mathematically verifiable state proofs, Universal Chain Verification (UCV-1) for heterogeneous proofs like BitVM and Trusted Execution Environments, and mempool orchestration for high-priority settlements via automated RBF/CPFP fee-bumping. The Gateway enforces strict mainnet-only branch promotion policies on its core branches, ensuring that no stubs or simulations enter production execution environments.
Conxian Nexus: The Observation and Proof Layer
The conxian-nexus repository serves as the primary observation, synchronization, and verification point for Tier 1 Chain Families, including Bitcoin, EVM-compatible chains, and Cosmos. Operating under a modular "Glass Node" architecture and currently in active development (v0.4.19), Nexus ingests multi-chain data and generates Merkle Mountain Range state root commitments for off-chain state. It ensures that authoritative off-chain state remains deterministically aligned with Layer 1 finality, providing the necessary proof baseline for the Gateway. Nexus also features the SRL-1 Lightning Resilience layer to maintain operational continuity and drift monitoring during sudden chain reorganizations.
Conxius Enclave SDK and lib-conxian-core
The lib-conxian-core repository (v0.3.1) provides the shared protocol primitives, trust tier taxonomies based on CON-791, anchoring models, and universal chain adapters for the entire ecosystem. Crucially, for hardware-backed signing, attestation, and BitVM2 operations, Conxian relies on the conxius-enclave-sdk (v2.0.11). This SDK provides the high-integrity root of trust required to physically isolate cryptographic signing from network observation, explicitly mitigating the vulnerability vectors exploited in the Kelp DAO incident. It utilizes advanced cryptography, including FROST Distributed Key Generation, though its 2.x production line mandates extreme caution and further audits prior to full value-bearing enablement.
Conxius Wallet and UI
The conxius-wallet (v1.9.5) provides a sovereign-first, Android-first reference client that unifies Bitcoin Layer 1 and emerging Layer 2 ecosystems behind hardware-isolated signing. It operates under a unique "Zero Secret Egress" privacy model, filtering data locally before network transmission to ensure no private cryptographic material leaves the sovereign device. The web application interface, conxian_ui, provides real-time protocol telemetry and institutional-grade interaction surfaces for the broader ecosystem, deploying robust node web services hosted strictly on compliant infrastructure.
